# How to cite this artifact.
#
# Citation File Format, read by GitHub and by Zenodo. It exists because the
# publication-process screen argues that without an institution behind it, the
# visible process is what makes a claim checkable — and then lists a citable
# identifier as one of the three things the screen was failing to provide.
#
# The `doi:` below is the DOI for *this version*, not the concept DOI that Zenodo
# also mints. The concept DOI resolves to whatever the newest version is, which is
# what the bare URL already did; the whole reason this artifact wanted an archived
# identifier was to distinguish one version from another, so the versioned one is
# the one recorded here and the concept DOI is listed under `identifiers` as what
# it is. The field was absent until an archive existed, on the grounds that claiming
# a DOI before one is minted is the kind of unearned confidence this project is
# about; it was added in its own commit, with the caveat on the process screen.
#
# The version and date below are the closed v0.7 entry in CHANGELOG.md. A citation
# of this artifact should name a version: the changelog records a retraction, so
# "the Drift Meter" without a version cannot distinguish the build that shipped an
# invented cohort dashboard from the build that removed it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you cite this artifact, please cite the version you read.
title: The Drift Meter
abstract: >-
  Experiment 01 of the Agential Drift Research Program. Three essay pages and one
  interactive instrument that asks a reader to complete the same evaluation task
  twice, once with an estimate supplied and once without, and reports a trace of
  how they worked rather than a score of whether they were right. A design
  argument rather than a finding: n is zero, no data has been collected from
  anyone, and every case figure is written for the exercise and disclosed as such.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pishtari
    given-names: Megi
    website: https://github.com/vigilia-mz
repository-code: https://github.com/vigilia-mz/drift-meter
url: https://vigilia-mz.github.io/drift-meter/
version: 0.7.0
date-released: '2026-08-10'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21887595
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21887595
    description: This version, v0.7.0.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21887594
    description: The concept DOI, which always resolves to the newest version.
# Two licences, deliberately, and REUSE.toml explains the split at length: the code
# under Apache-2.0, and the prose — the essays, every word of screen copy, the
# system prompts, the changelog and the source table — under CC BY 4.0.
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - research artifact
  - human-AI interaction
  - automation bias
  - deskilling
  - pre-registration
